Peanut Butter Chilli Chicken Bowl — absolute flavour town. Not a boring chicken salad.

Full Recipe (1 serving)
* Sliced cucumber — 125g
* Peanut butter — 18g
* Honey — 10g
* Garlic — 1 tsp
* Chilli oil — 12g
* Soy sauce — 1 tbsp
* Lime — ½, squeezed
* Cabbage — 50g
* Cooked chicken — 150g
* Sesame seeds — ½ tsp

Cook chicken however you like — air fry, pan fry, poach, oven bake or rotisserie all work. Combine all sauce ingredients and toss everything together in a bowl.

Macros
* Calories: 451
* Protein: 43g
* Carbs: 14g
* Fat: 26g

Verdict
9.5/10 — One of the highest scores on the series and it’s fully deserved. The peanut butter, chilli oil, soy and lime dressing is an elite combination that turns a chicken salad into something genuinely exciting. If you like peanut butter you have to try this — the extra calories from it are absolutely worth every single one. The cucumber and cabbage add great crunch and volume, and 43g of protein for 451 calories is a brilliant macro split on top of everything else. This is what mixing up your lunch rotation looks like.

