✅ Worth the Hype (9.5/10)

High Protein Carrot Cake Loaf — and I’d say I’m a qualified judge. My wedding cake was a carrot cake.

Full Recipe (makes 16 slices)
• Carrots, grated — 200g
• Whole eggs — 2
• High protein Greek yogurt — 150g
• Vanilla protein powder — 60g
• Plain flour — 100g
• Extra light milk — 100ml
• Vanilla extract — 5ml
• Cinnamon — 1 tsp
• Stevia sweetener — 10g
• Baking powder — 1 tsp
• Baking soda — 1 tsp
• Salt — 1 tsp
• Olive oil — small drizzle

Add everything into a bowl and mix until smooth. Fold through the grated carrot, pour into a lined loaf tin and bake at 180°C for 25 minutes. Let it cool before slicing — trust me it’s worth the wait.

Macros (per slice)
• Calories: 62
• Protein: 6g
• Carbs: 7g
• Fat: 1g
Macros (whole loaf)
• Calories: 985
• Protein: 97g
• Carbs: 119g
• Fat: 19g

Verdict
9.5/10 — one of the best things I’ve made in this series. Soft, moist and packed with that warm cinnamon and carrot flavour that makes carrot cake what it is. And that’s without any icing. My wedding cake was a carrot cake so I don’t say this lightly — this is genuinely incredible for a healthy high protein version. 62 calories a slice and 6g protein. Perfect with a coffee or whenever you want something sweet that still fits your calories.

