✅ Worth the Hype (9.5/10)

Air Fried Protein Cheese Bites — better than some garlic breads I’ve had in restaurants. No joke.
Full Recipe
• Finely shredded parmesan cheese — 170g (6oz)
• Egg whites — 65g

Mix the parmesan and egg whites together thoroughly. Roll into tight 1 inch balls. Lay on a sheet pan and freeze for 2 hours. Air fry at 200°C for 10 minutes. Dip into marinara or any sauce you like and enjoy.

Macros (full batch)
• Calories: ~620
• Protein: ~52g
• Carbs: ~4g
• Fat: ~44g

Per bite (approx 10 bites)
• Calories: ~62
• Protein: ~5g
• Carbs: ~0g
• Fat: ~4g

Verdict
9.5/10 — I went in skeptical and came out a believer. Two ingredients, zero carbs and they come out of the air fryer crispy on the outside and gooey in the middle. Dipped in marinara these genuinely rival garlic bread you’d get in a restaurant. The 2 hour freeze is the only thing standing between this and a perfect score — plan ahead and you won’t regret it.

