Breakfast Bagels (Bacon, Egg & Cheese!) — Best savoury breakfast I’ve ever made. This was elite! Normally rice paper is soft, but this was crispy, cheesy, salty, savoury, and divine.

Full Recipe (Per bagel)
* Egg — 1 scrambled (approx. 50g / 1.8 oz) / can use just egg white to further reduce calories!
* Bacon medallion — 1 medallion (approx. 25g / 0.9 oz)
* Reduced-fat mozzarella cheese — a sprinkle (approx. 20g / 0.7 oz / 2 tbsp)
* Rice paper — 1 sheet (approx. 10g / 0.3 oz), dipped in egg

Method:
1. Scramble your egg.
2. Cook your bacon medallion.
3. Dip 1 sheet of rice paper in egg, assemble with the scrambled egg, bacon medallion, and a sprinkle of reduced-fat mozzarella cheese, then fold or wrap it up.
4. Cook/crisp it up until golden and crunchy.

Macros (per bagel)
* Calories: 220 cals
* Protein: 22g
* Carbs: 11g
* Fat: 10g

Verdict
9/10 — Easily the best savoury breakfast I’ve ever made. This was completely elite. Normally rice paper stays soft and chewy, but this technique makes it wonderfully crispy, cheesy, salty, savoury, and divine. If you haven’t tried this yet, you need to.

